.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT.CREATECAPTION" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement.createCaption \- HTMLTableElement: createCaption()
method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]createCaption()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface creates a \f[CR]<caption>\f[R]
element, inserts it as the first child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R],
and returns it.
If the table already has a \f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element child, this
method returns the first such child without creating one.
.PP
When creation is needed, this method creates and inserts the element
directly, without requiring separate calls to methods such as
\f[CR]Document.createElement()\f[R] and \f[CR]Node.insertBefore()\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
createCaption()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
An \f[CR]HTMLTableCaptionElement\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
This example uses JavaScript to add a caption to a table that initially
lacks one.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]table\f[R]>
  <\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 1.1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 1.2</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 1.3</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 2.1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 2.2</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Cell 2.3</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
  </\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
</\f[B]table\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] table = document.querySelector(\(dqtable\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] caption = table.createCaption();
caption.textContent = \(dqThis caption was created by JavaScript!\(dq;
.EE
.SS Result
